This appears to be a CBP ruling on the body of a digital torpedo level, a polycarbonate body with a magnet that is imported as a component. The completed level would fall under 9015.80 (other surveying/measuring instruments) or 9031.49 (other optical measuring instruments). Spirit levels are classified in 9015.30. The completed digital level with bubble vials is a level under 9015.30.8000 (levels other than optical). Parts of those instruments go under 9015.90.0140 or 9015.90.0160.

The body is a part of a level. It is not a general plastic article, because it is dedicated to forming the level and is precisely made for it. I recall that CBP ruled this was classified under 9015.90.0160. I am not certain of the final digits. The HTS 9015.90.01 covers parts and accessories, with 9015.90.0140 for "other" parts and 9015.90.0160 as the other subheading. I believe 9015.90.0160 is the correct one, so I am going with it.

{"hts_code": "9015.90.0160", "reason": "The pre-formed polycarbonate body is a dedicated part of a non-optical level (heading 9015, spirit levels of 9015.30), so it is classified as a part of surveying/measuring instruments in 9015.90."}
